    "type": "question",
    "label": "",
    "prompt": "The cost of a helicopter ride is $\\$59$ plus $\\$12$ per km. Form an inequality to find the greatest number of whole kilometres you can ride in the helicopter with a budget of $\\$150$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$12n+59\\le150$; greatest whole-number distance: $7\\text{ km}$.",
      "worked": "Let $n$ be the number of kilometres travelled.\n$$\\begin{align*}12n+59&\\le150\\\\12n&\\le91\\\\n&\\le\\frac{91}{12}\\end{align*}$$\nSince $n$ must be a whole number, the greatest distance is $7\\text{ km}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
